cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use picasso, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "picasso: self-contained Nix flakes for scientific and agentic toolchains, and the NixOS workstation they run on"
abstract: >-
  picasso, formerly nix-config, is a set of self-contained Nix flakes, called labs, that pin the
  toolchains a computational ocean-science and software project needs: WAVEWATCH III with
  gfortran, OpenMPI and NetCDF (pratico), a pandoc and TeX Live publishing pipeline with its own
  GitHub Action (publisher), a lint set (lint), a sandbox and helpers for coding agents (agentic),
  a CUDA and PyTorch host setup (cuda), and a presenter's desk for screen annotation, capture and
  webcam profiles (present). Each lab references nothing outside its own directory, commits its
  lock file, and exports the same outputs, so another repository can borrow one as a flake input,
  a sparse git submodule or a GitHub Action and get the same toolchain on any machine and in CI.
  CI builds every lab's checks in the Nix sandbox on every push.

  The same repository defines the author's NixOS workstation and a one-command virtual machine for
  trying it from another Linux system. It is the toolchain layer under WW3 GPU Lab and marola,
  which consume its labs.
